# pnpm 11 ignores `node-linker` set here. This file used to set
# `node-linker=hoisted` and claim that mattered; the installed layout was
# isolated the whole time. Check `node_modules/.modules.yaml` for what pnpm
# actually did rather than trusting a setting in this file.
#
# The isolated layout is fine, and for a reason worth writing down. Extensions
# are loaded into pi's own process, so they must not each end up with their own
# copy of a shared dependency. They do not: seven extensions declare `effect`,
# and every one of their `node_modules/effect` entries is a symlink into the
# same `.pnpm/effect@<version>` directory. Node resolves a symlink before
# caching a module, so all seven share one instance and the graph is parsed
# once — which is the property the startup work depended on.
#
# The pi SDK is deliberately declared by no extension at all. It comes from the
# root install, so an extension always uses the same instance pi is running.
# SETUP.md has the `~/.pi/agent/node_modules` symlink that makes that resolve.
#
# Kept for the explanation. There is nothing to configure.
